#EXTM3U
# M4-01 matcher fixture (D-EPG-2). One row per strategy, per ambiguity rule
# and per <display-name> shape; the guide side is tests/fixtures/epg-match.xml
# and the expected counts are tests/fixtures/epg-match.json. Do not reorder:
# the playlist order decides which row wins a feed base, and the Multi row
# depends on it. Append, do not insert.
#
# The last six rows were added on 2026-10-03 for the review of the M4 round.
# "Noise Channel (1080p) [Geo-blocked]" and "Guide Marker Channel" are the
# two rows the SEARCH key cannot match -- one carries the markers on OUR
# side, the other on the GUIDE's -- so between them they make each of
# M4-01's two epg_name_key call sites revertible-red; the
# Number First and Lang rows are guides whose first <display-name> is not the
# name; Markup and Sink are M4-02 sinks (a <desc> with a child element, and a
# <desc> whose cap cut lands inside a URL's userinfo).
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="Exact.us" group-title="Match",Exact Channel
http://stream.example.test/exact.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="Suffix.us@SD" group-title="Match",Suffix Channel
http://stream.example.test/suffix.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="Bare.us" group-title="Match",Bare Channel
http://stream.example.test/bare.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="namehit.xx" group-title="Match",Name Only Channel
http://stream.example.test/namehit.m3u8
